# AI Behavior

## Defaults

- Prefer small, targeted diffs that match existing patterns.
- Read nearby code and shared packages before inventing new abstractions.
- Use `@npha/shared` schemas/types/permissions instead of duplicating them.
- Keep scoring math inside `@npha/scoring-engine`; keep Prisma in services.

## When fixing bugs

- Trace API shape ↔ UI assumptions (null country, nested pilot, pagination max 200).
- For auth failures on downloads/exports, check Bearer + blob pattern first.
- For “CSS broken” in admin after reports, suspect unscoped injected HTML before rewriting the design system.

## Do not

- Commit unless the user asks; do not force-push or skip hooks.
- Add unsolicited markdown docs or README sprawl — update existing `docs/` when needed.
- Start long-running `npm run dev` unless the user needs it or servers are down for the task.
- Mention these rule files unless asked.

## Product judgment

- Product is **AeroJudge** (Nepalabs) — commercial SaaS quality, not demo software.
- Never hardcode Nepal, NPHA, organizations, sponsors, or countries; use configurable settings / reference data.
- Settings-driven FAI flexibility over rigid Cat 1 defaults.
- Explicit publish; dual approval before locking official scores when settings require it.
